{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The maximum magnitude outcome for both lotteries is the positive non-zero outcome, as these are the highest absolute values (2500 Euros for Lottery B and 2400 Euros for Lottery A). The probabilities of these outcomes are 33% for Lottery B and 34% for Lottery A. The reason evaluates which lottery has the more favorable maximum magnitude outcome weighted by its probability. In this case, Lottery B has a higher outcome (2500 > 2400) but a slightly lower probability (33% < 34%). The weighted values would be 2500 × 0.33 = 825 and 2400 × 0.34 = 816. Thus, the reason would favor Lottery B due to the higher weighted maximum magnitude outcome.",
